1
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:04,693
You've got something in your hair.

2
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:06,033
Huh?

3
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:09,267
Hold on.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,533
Cabbage. Kamekichi's food.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,400
That's hilarious.

6
00:01:03,867 --> 00:01:05,467
Delivery!

7
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:08,167
Coming!

8
00:01:11,767 --> 00:01:12,767
Here's your package.

9
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:14,400
Thanks.

10
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:20,667
Okay.

11
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:22,067
Thank you.

12
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:38,367
Ouch!

13
00:01:42,067 --> 00:01:44,533
What should I do?

14
00:02:25,067 --> 00:02:28,400
"Duty First, Kiss Later"

15
00:02:29,767 --> 00:02:33,400
(Episode 4)

16
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:46,000
Good morning.

17
00:02:47,633 --> 00:02:48,700
Morning.

18
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,667
You're awfully quiet today.

19
00:03:00,133 --> 00:03:01,600
Am I?

20
00:03:02,467 --> 00:03:05,167
You were so forward yesterday.

21
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,767
You even kissed...

22
00:03:13,267 --> 00:03:15,033
You even tried to kiss me...

23
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,900
What on earth should I do?

24
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,800
What am I supposed to do?

25
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,400
I'm going to deliver these documents.

26
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,000
Take care.

27
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:30,433
Okay.

28
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:39,267
I saw that.

29
00:03:39,367 --> 00:03:40,067
Huh?

30
00:03:40,167 --> 00:03:42,800
You guys finally came to work together.

31
00:03:43,633 --> 00:03:45,767
It... It was just a coincidence.

32
00:03:45,867 --> 00:03:48,133
Really?

33
00:03:48,233 --> 00:03:50,367
We live in the same place.

34
00:03:50,467 --> 00:03:52,633
It's normal to come together sometimes.

35
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:56,233
Alright, let's just go with that.

36
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:57,567
What?

37
00:04:07,567 --> 00:04:09,200
Takoi.

38
00:04:09,767 --> 00:04:11,800
She's here again today.

39
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:12,567
Hello.

40
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:13,867
Ah, Hikari-chan.

41
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:15,167
Hi there.

42
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:18,867
What are we doing today?

43
00:04:19,333 --> 00:04:22,667
Oh, Hikari-chan is here again today?

44
00:04:22,767 --> 00:04:25,076
- Can you draw with me?
- It must be hard for her without her dad.

45
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:25,867
- Yeah.
- Let's go.

46
00:04:25,967 --> 00:04:29,333
She comes to see Takoi almost every day.

47
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:32,933
It's tough being a popular guy.

48
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:38,700
Go call him over.

49
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,467
He's the culprit.

50
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:46,376
- It's so hard to choose.
- Is it?

51
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,933
Haven't you decided yet?

52
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:50,133
Which one should I pick?

53
00:04:57,867 --> 00:04:59,000
Here, some juice.

54
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:00,267
Thank you.

55
00:05:05,267 --> 00:05:06,700
What about school?

56
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:12,000
I wanted to go, but I couldn't.

57
00:05:14,067 --> 00:05:15,633
I see.

58
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,567
Look.

59
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,000
Huh? Is that...

60
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,433
It's Takoi.

61
00:05:27,533 --> 00:05:28,933
Huh?

62
00:05:29,033 --> 00:05:30,733
Am I really that handsome?

63
00:05:30,833 --> 00:05:31,700
Yeah.

64
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,700
Takoi is handsome.

65
00:05:35,133 --> 00:05:37,433
Thanks, perfect score.

66
00:05:37,533 --> 00:05:39,033
Yeah.

67
00:05:41,167 --> 00:05:42,000
Hey.
Hmm?

68
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:47,067
When will my dad be released?

69
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:48,633
Huh?

70
00:05:48,733 --> 00:05:50,267
Will it be soon?

71
00:05:50,367 --> 00:05:52,100
Will it take a long time?

72
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:57,833
Well...

73
00:05:58,767 --> 00:06:00,133
He'll be back soon.

74
00:06:00,233 --> 00:06:02,167
Just wait a little longer.

75
00:06:02,267 --> 00:06:02,733
Okay.

76
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:04,300
Yeah.

77
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,667
Here you go.

78
00:06:07,767 --> 00:06:09,167
Thanks.

79
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:11,067
- Looking good.
- Right?

80
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:12,667
You drew it so carefully.

81
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:16,967
I'll be going now.

82
00:06:20,533 --> 00:06:21,967
Good work today.

83
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:24,033
Well then, good work.

84
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:25,133
- Hey.
- Yeah?

85
00:06:25,233 --> 00:06:26,367
Let's go grab a drink today.

86
00:06:26,467 --> 00:06:27,467
Uh...

87
00:06:27,533 --> 00:06:28,367
Good work...
Ah, Yagi.

88
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:31,467
I'm having dinner with my
daughter's boyfriend today.

89
00:06:31,567 --> 00:06:33,233
- Good work.
- Good work.

90
00:06:33,667 --> 00:06:34,533
Tonight...

91
00:06:34,633 --> 00:06:36,333
Your wife's birthday was last week, right?

92
00:06:36,433 --> 00:06:38,333
- Good work.
- Egawa.

93
00:06:38,433 --> 00:06:40,767
- Good work.
- Good work.

94
00:06:42,267 --> 00:06:44,800
- Alright, I'll go.
- That's great.

95
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:45,800
What's so great about it?

96
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:48,533
No, I just don't want to
go home too early today.

97
00:06:48,633 --> 00:06:50,609
That doesn't sound like
something a married man would say.

98
00:06:50,633 --> 00:06:51,733
Let's go.

99
00:06:51,833 --> 00:06:52,933
Awesome!

100
00:06:53,033 --> 00:06:54,567
Just one drink, seriously, just one.

101
00:06:54,667 --> 00:06:56,976
Every time you say "just one,"
we end up drinking for ages.

102
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
No, we won't.

103
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:01,667
Oh, welcome.

104
00:07:03,667 --> 00:07:05,633
Huh? Why?

105
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,467
Oh, Shiono.

106
00:07:07,567 --> 00:07:08,567
Rare to see you alone.

107
00:07:08,633 --> 00:07:09,300
Yeah.

108
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,500
I felt like eating out for a change.

109
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,867
What a coincidence.

110
00:07:12,967 --> 00:07:14,467
Drinking with Takoi is boring anyway.

111
00:07:14,567 --> 00:07:16,233
But it's different with you here, Shiono.

112
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:17,600
Want to drink together?

113
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,833
- Is that okay?
- What?

114
00:07:18,933 --> 00:07:20,033
I'd love to.

115
00:07:20,133 --> 00:07:21,633
Ah, sorry.

116
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:23,867
I have to visit my hometown today.

117
00:07:23,967 --> 00:07:25,433
Hold on.

118
00:07:25,533 --> 00:07:27,867
You're under arrest.

119
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:31,667
Isn't your hometown really far away?

120
00:07:34,833 --> 00:07:36,567
Cheers.

121
00:07:39,633 --> 00:07:41,843
Come to think of it, this is our
first time drinking together like this.

122
00:07:41,867 --> 00:07:42,633
Yeah.

123
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:44,500
We don't usually get a chance to talk.

124
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,400
What about Takoi?

125
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,867
Huh?

126
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:51,733
Well, I've never had a meal with him.

127
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:52,200
I see.

128
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:55,100
But we've done much more intimate things.

129
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,967
What do you mean by "more intimate things"?

130
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:00,100
It's nothing.

131
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:05,233
We just live next door
to each other, that's all.

132
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:06,700
Exactly.

133
00:08:14,467 --> 00:08:16,500
The two of us really...

134
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,067
haven't done anything, right?

135
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:21,533
I see.

136
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:24,667
Boss, get me a beer.

137
00:08:24,767 --> 00:08:25,767
You got it. Welcome.

138
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,800
Oh my.

139
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:28,733
- Oh, long time no see.
- Hasegawa.

140
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:29,533
Long time no see.
Hiro.

141
00:08:30,533 --> 00:08:31,533
Let's talk over here.

142
00:08:31,633 --> 00:08:32,900
Huh?

143
00:08:35,367 --> 00:08:36,567
Seriously, man.

144
00:08:36,667 --> 00:08:37,700
What?

145
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,600
What do you mean, "what"?

146
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,233
Man.

147
00:08:47,767 --> 00:08:50,667
I was hoping to drink with you alone.

148
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:58,733
- Here you go.
- Great, thanks.

149
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:00,133
Thanks.

150
00:09:03,067 --> 00:09:05,767
You're so gentle with Hikari-chan.

151
00:09:06,267 --> 00:09:08,800
Be a little gentler with me too.

152
00:09:10,867 --> 00:09:12,300
Idiot!

153
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:13,743
Hikari-chan is only in this
situation because of you.

154
00:09:13,767 --> 00:09:16,367
Oh, Hikari-chan.

155
00:09:16,467 --> 00:09:18,467
I feel pretty bad for her.

156
00:09:19,967 --> 00:09:21,067
Speaking of her...

157
00:09:21,367 --> 00:09:25,867
The reason she comes to see Takoi is probably
because she misses her dad and feels lonely.

158
00:09:27,533 --> 00:09:32,267
After all, I promised to help her.

159
00:09:33,267 --> 00:09:35,767
But giving her unrealistic expectations...

160
00:09:35,867 --> 00:09:37,367
Is that really a good idea?

161
00:09:37,467 --> 00:09:38,867
Huh?

162
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:42,700
Hikari-chan's dad is suspected
of another case of fraud.

163
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,933
He's still being interrogated.

164
00:09:46,933 --> 00:09:49,867
Right now, there's only
eyewitness testimony, right?

165
00:09:49,967 --> 00:09:51,733
- But...
- She finally...

166
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:54,233
Started smiling again.

167
00:09:54,333 --> 00:09:56,567
And finally got her spirits back.

168
00:09:56,667 --> 00:09:59,500
I just don't want things to
take a turn for the worse...

169
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,467
And strip away all her hope.

170
00:10:01,567 --> 00:10:03,733
What if something goes wrong?

171
00:10:04,867 --> 00:10:07,067
You gave her hope.

172
00:10:07,367 --> 00:10:10,033
Can you take responsibility in the end?

173
00:10:15,467 --> 00:10:17,227
What about you? Did
you take responsibility?

174
00:10:17,667 --> 00:10:18,467
Huh?

175
00:10:18,567 --> 00:10:22,167
Calling her dad a criminal
right in front of her...

176
00:10:22,267 --> 00:10:23,833
You completely broke her heart!

177
00:10:23,933 --> 00:10:25,667
But that's...

178
00:10:25,767 --> 00:10:28,409
- The truth, right?
- Does being the truth make it okay to hurt her?

179
00:10:28,433 --> 00:10:30,267
Alright, alright...

180
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:32,600
You only care about reading the room.

181
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:34,933
Giving someone false hope is even crueler.

182
00:10:36,167 --> 00:10:39,567
Do you know what it
feels like to be let down?

183
00:10:44,433 --> 00:10:45,567
Boss!

184
00:10:45,667 --> 00:10:47,300
Give me two orders of thick fried tofu.

185
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,733
Hey! You still haven't had enough?

186
00:10:49,833 --> 00:10:51,143
Because the mood in here is freezing.

187
00:10:51,167 --> 00:10:51,967
Good one.

188
00:10:52,067 --> 00:10:53,233
That was way too intense.

189
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:54,333
Oh.

190
00:10:55,767 --> 00:10:57,433
Hey, Takoi!

191
00:10:58,633 --> 00:10:59,933
You haven't paid yet!

192
00:11:08,633 --> 00:11:10,733
Huh? With Shiono?

193
00:11:10,833 --> 00:11:11,533
Yeah.

194
00:11:11,733 --> 00:11:13,133
For Yuki's interrogation...

195
00:11:13,233 --> 00:11:15,300
I asked the Community
Safety Division for backup.

196
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:17,333
I heard Shiono volunteered to go.

197
00:11:17,433 --> 00:11:18,700
But...

198
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:21,033
We've been swamped lately too.

199
00:11:21,467 --> 00:11:22,900
Isn't that a good thing?

200
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,967
It's easier to get things
done with two people.

201
00:11:25,067 --> 00:11:27,000
Especially since it's Shiono.

202
00:11:27,267 --> 00:11:31,767
For Hikari-chan's sake, we
need to clear this case up quickly.

203
00:11:31,867 --> 00:11:33,767
I'm counting on you, Takoi.

204
00:11:33,867 --> 00:11:35,400
Counting on you.

205
00:11:41,533 --> 00:11:43,467
Around 2:00 PM on the 6th,

206
00:11:43,567 --> 00:11:47,700
you were seen near Kakegawa-san's house.

207
00:11:49,733 --> 00:11:51,367
Yuki-san.

208
00:11:51,733 --> 00:11:53,767
What were you doing there that day?

209
00:11:54,633 --> 00:11:56,933
I was on my break from work.

210
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:01,500
That's pretty far from
your workplace, isn't it?

211
00:12:03,533 --> 00:12:06,767
Were you scouting a
location for your crime?

212
00:12:11,467 --> 00:12:13,067
One more thing.

213
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:15,867
At 3:00 PM on the 17th.

214
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:19,400
I heard you had the day off.

215
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:21,300
What were you doing?

216
00:12:23,933 --> 00:12:25,733
I don't really remember.

217
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,533
Listen to me.

218
00:12:31,633 --> 00:12:34,633
For Hikari-chan's sake,
you better think hard.

219
00:12:34,733 --> 00:12:35,633
If you keep saying you don't remember,

220
00:12:35,733 --> 00:12:37,933
it's going to work against you later.

221
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:41,600
Hikari-chan is waiting for you too.

222
00:12:42,667 --> 00:12:43,667
You know?

223
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,867
If you're lying, things
will get very serious.

224
00:12:52,967 --> 00:12:56,533
You've already been arrested for assault.

225
00:12:58,167 --> 00:13:01,067
If we find more evidence,

226
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:04,967
you can kiss the life you wanted goodbye.

227
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,333
Excuse me.

228
00:13:14,433 --> 00:13:16,067
Takoi, come here for a second.

229
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,733
On the 17th, the day of the incident.

230
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:22,533
The security camera caught it.

231
00:13:27,467 --> 00:13:30,500
The camera at the house
across the street caught this.

232
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:33,967
The person in this footage is you, right?

233
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,933
Damn it!

234
00:13:39,733 --> 00:13:40,833
Yuki...

235
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,976
Do you have any idea how
much Hikari-chan is suffering?!

236
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,600
Do you realize what you've done?

237
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:48,833
- Calm down.
- Hikari-chan is...

238
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:50,167
Takoi.

239
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:56,167
Hikari-chan.

240
00:13:59,867 --> 00:14:01,467
I'm sorry.

241
00:14:03,333 --> 00:14:05,167
About your dad, I...

242
00:14:05,267 --> 00:14:06,800
Liar.

243
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,500
Liar!

244
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:13,400
You said my dad would be back soon!

245
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:15,700
Hikari-chan...

246
00:14:15,767 --> 00:14:16,933
I hate you.

247
00:14:17,033 --> 00:14:18,867
I hate you so much!

248
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,667
Didn't I tell you before?

249
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,000
It's your kindness, Takoi,

250
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:29,167
that ended up hurting Hikari-chan.

251
00:14:33,633 --> 00:14:35,833
You knew from the start, didn't you?

252
00:14:35,933 --> 00:14:39,100
It would only force this
child to face a harsher reality.

253
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:43,533
Is this the hope you were talking about?

254
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:46,200
The hope you speak of
is nothing but despair for her.

255
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:51,400
Giving her expectations
only hurt her more...

256
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:52,967
Shut up!

257
00:14:55,267 --> 00:14:58,467
And losing control in front of a child...

258
00:14:58,567 --> 00:15:00,400
Is that supposed to be hope too?

259
00:15:22,967 --> 00:15:24,207
(Yamma-no-michi Police Station)

260
00:15:24,267 --> 00:15:25,600
Good work on your shift.

261
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,000
Ouch.

262
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:32,033
Stop bullying Takoi!

263
00:15:32,133 --> 00:15:33,233
Huh?

264
00:15:33,333 --> 00:15:36,567
If you bully Takoi again,
I'll never forgive you!

265
00:15:36,667 --> 00:15:37,533
Hikari-chan?

266
00:15:37,633 --> 00:15:38,900
Wait a minute!

267
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:54,933
Um...

268
00:16:06,067 --> 00:16:07,100
Are you hungry?

269
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,333
Yeah.

270
00:16:08,433 --> 00:16:09,633
I'm hungry.

271
00:16:09,733 --> 00:16:11,333
What should we eat then?

272
00:16:15,333 --> 00:16:16,733
Yuki-san.

273
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:24,067
I'm sorry about last time.

274
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,267
It's fine now.

275
00:16:29,367 --> 00:16:30,667
Huh?

276
00:16:32,333 --> 00:16:35,300
I'm sorry I said I hated you.

277
00:16:36,733 --> 00:16:39,000
I heard you've been
taking great care of her.

278
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,343
I'm really sorry for the trouble.

279
00:16:40,367 --> 00:16:41,367
Not at all.

280
00:16:42,433 --> 00:16:43,600
Are you doing okay?

281
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:47,233
I mean, about your husband.

282
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:50,233
I've decided to get a divorce.

283
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:53,133
I'm taking her back to my parents' house.

284
00:16:53,233 --> 00:16:55,133
We just came to say goodbye today.

285
00:16:56,833 --> 00:16:58,600
I see.

286
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:00,733
Yeah.

287
00:17:01,067 --> 00:17:01,967
You know...

288
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:03,833
Don't look so down.

289
00:17:03,933 --> 00:17:06,833
I feel a lot better now.

290
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:11,300
And I don't want to make her sad anymore.

291
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,867
That makes sense.

292
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:16,367
Oh.

293
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,933
Shiono came by this morning.

294
00:17:22,033 --> 00:17:23,167
Huh?

295
00:17:27,233 --> 00:17:28,667
What?

296
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:31,567
You came all the way just to drop this off?

297
00:17:31,667 --> 00:17:32,900
Yes.

298
00:17:34,767 --> 00:17:36,167
Also,

299
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:39,867
I wanted to apologize to both of you.

300
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:41,667
Huh?

301
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,867
I'm sorry.

302
00:17:51,533 --> 00:17:57,200
I can't believe I said a terrible thing about
her dad being a criminal in front of Hikari-chan.

303
00:18:01,233 --> 00:18:02,667
It's okay.

304
00:18:03,033 --> 00:18:07,100
It's the truth anyway. He
brought it upon himself.

305
00:18:20,867 --> 00:18:22,367
Hikari-chan.

306
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,533
I'm truly sorry.

307
00:18:28,833 --> 00:18:32,333
And about yesterday,

308
00:18:36,033 --> 00:18:39,367
I think I can understand how you feel.

309
00:18:41,433 --> 00:18:42,633
Because I'm just like you.

310
00:18:42,733 --> 00:18:44,333
Just like Hikari-chan.

311
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:46,533
Huh?

312
00:18:48,367 --> 00:18:50,467
Having expectations for someone important,

313
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,200
but feeling so lonely at the same time.

314
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:57,133
That's why I said those things.

315
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,933
Like me?

316
00:19:00,033 --> 00:19:01,800
Are you lonely too?

317
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,900
Yeah.

318
00:19:05,533 --> 00:19:06,967
Why?

319
00:19:10,333 --> 00:19:12,167
Because...

320
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:16,433
even though I like Takoi too,

321
00:19:17,533 --> 00:19:19,833
he only pays attention to Hikari-chan.

322
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,067
I felt so jealous.

323
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:33,867
Shiono?

324
00:19:34,167 --> 00:19:35,767
I heard he's not around right now.

325
00:19:35,867 --> 00:19:38,900
Yeah, he went to headquarters.

326
00:19:39,433 --> 00:19:42,400
But I'm glad I got to see you, Takoi.

327
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:44,600
Thank you, Takoi.

328
00:19:46,867 --> 00:19:48,333
I should be the one thanking you.

329
00:19:50,033 --> 00:19:51,467
And...

330
00:19:52,867 --> 00:19:54,200
Please wait a moment...

331
00:19:58,767 --> 00:20:01,067
Please give this to Shiono for me.

332
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:06,900
"Shiono, I'm sorry for kicking you.
Make up with Takoi, okay? Hikari-chan."

333
00:20:16,933 --> 00:20:17,833
That's so sweet of you.

334
00:20:17,933 --> 00:20:19,267
Yeah.

335
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,700
I'm such an idiot...

336
00:20:28,767 --> 00:20:31,133
What the hell am I doing?

337
00:20:32,033 --> 00:20:33,467
Here you go.

338
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:38,033
Hey.

339
00:20:38,233 --> 00:20:40,367
I don't know what's eating you,

340
00:20:40,767 --> 00:20:42,167
but just sitting there overthinking

341
00:20:42,233 --> 00:20:45,600
isn't going to solve anything, is it?

342
00:20:45,700 --> 00:20:46,900
Huh?

343
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:50,400
Takoi Heisuke isn't exactly
the brains of the operation.

344
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,367
You're a man of action.

345
00:20:53,067 --> 00:20:55,333
You either apologize or say thank you.

346
00:20:55,433 --> 00:20:56,733
It's one or the other.

347
00:20:56,833 --> 00:20:58,400
Simple as that, right?

348
00:21:02,033 --> 00:21:04,300
Oh, by the way, Takoi.

349
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:05,700
Do you want these?

350
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:10,867
(Izu Mito Sea Paradise)

351
00:21:10,967 --> 00:21:13,867
Someone gave them to me,
but I'm not going to use them.

352
00:21:13,967 --> 00:21:15,100
Take them and go on a date.

353
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:16,400
How about it?

354
00:21:24,033 --> 00:21:25,433
Boss, sorry.

355
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:26,533
Please cancel my order.

356
00:21:26,633 --> 00:21:29,033
- Huh?
- Put it on my tab. I'll pay next time.

357
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:33,300
That guy really can't sit still.

358
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,167
Let's charge him double then.

359
00:21:35,933 --> 00:21:36,933
Sounds good.

360
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:43,200
Shiono.

361
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,533
What's up?

362
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:49,200
I'm sorry.

363
00:21:52,467 --> 00:21:53,867
And...

364
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:59,833
Thank you for what you did for Hikari-chan.

365
00:22:05,867 --> 00:22:07,700
I l-

366
00:22:08,867 --> 00:22:10,400
I like...

367
00:22:10,867 --> 00:22:12,000
Huh?

368
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:13,900
- I like y-...
- What?

369
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:21,167
Do you want to go to the aquarium?

370
00:22:29,933 --> 00:22:32,533
(This drama is purely fictional)

371
00:22:32,967 --> 00:22:34,800
(Next Episode)
It's huge!

372
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,400
I want Takoi to have a good time.

373
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:38,340
After all, it's a date
with someone important.

374
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,100
You're finally going after men too?

375
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:43,000
Why would I ever date a guy?

376
00:22:43,100 --> 00:22:44,800
Hurry up!
